<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov raw sugar imports down 15.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov raw sugar imports down 15.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in November totalled 167,719 tonnes, down 15.8 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Nov 96	Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p> Total		  167,719     201,448	  199,238</p>
<p>Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		 6,987	39,106	   23,628</p>
<p> South Africa	  38,001	53,094	   37,481</p>
<p> Australia	    114,133	86,034	  138,129</p>
<p> Fiji		     8,598	23,214		nil</p>
<p> Cuba			 nil	   nil		nil</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first 11 months of this year totalled 1,516,909 tonnes against 1,610,309 tonnes during the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
